From d78d8e14fa9f67d33487c1a10292bb243dd9d774 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: agent-keys <noreply@agent-keys.invalid>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:53:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] fix(operator): a Safe module is authority too -- no
 handover while the agent EOA is one

`assertAgentEoaHasNoAuthority` and `jinn signer-migrate` looked at the Safe's
owners and at the agent NFT only. A module is not an owner:
`execTransactionFromModule` runs any call or delegatecall from the Safe for an
enabled module, with no owner's signature, and `swapOwner` does not remove it.
A keystore EOA that was a module of the Safe kept the Safe after a migration
that reported "the EOA has no authority" (the internal audit of 2026-11-28,
finding AK-2026-11-28-02).

- signer/attestation.ts: readSafeModuleAuthority reads the Safe's modules
  (`isModuleEnabled(eoa)` and the whole `getModulesPaginated` list; it goes on
  from the last module read, because Safe 1.3.0 returns the following page's
  first module as `next` and a read that starts there leaves it out).
  assertAgentEoaHasNoAuthority refuses while the EOA is an enabled module and
  resolves with the Safe's other modules.
- signer/migrate.ts: a first step, `safe-modules`, before anything changes
  hands and in a dry run too. It refuses while the EOA is a module; every
  other module is listed with the status `review` (and in `modules`), for the
  operator to review: each has the same power over the Safe.
- main.ts: at boot the daemon warns about each other module.
- tests: unit (the EOA as a module; other modules named; paging as Safe 1.3.0
  and 1.4.1 do it; a list that does not end). On Safe 1.3.0's own bytecode,
  test/hermetic/signer-migrate-refusals.test.ts: the migration refuses and
  nothing is swapped; after a swap done by hand the former owner still pays
  out of the Safe and neither the check nor a re-run reports that Safe as
  handed over; three modules are listed across pages.
- test/hermetic/full-loop-kernel-owner.test.ts: on Jinn's snapshot the staked
  service Safe has modules already (stOLAS creates it with the distributor and
  its guard enabled, next to the recovery module), none of them the agent EOA:
  the step reports `review` and names each, and the loop asserts both.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
